<title>USA: US March leading indicators +0.1 pct-Conference Bd.</title>
<headline>US March leading indicators +0.1 pct-Conference Bd.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Conference Board index of leading, coincident and lagging indicators (1992=100) and percent changes from previous months, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>Indicators: Index--March  Feb (Prev)  Jan (Prev)  Dec (Prev)</p>
<p> -Leading    103.6   0.1   0.5   0.5   0.3   0.3   0.1  Unch</p>
<p> -Coincident 115.4   0.3   0.6   0.4   0.3   0.3   0.3   0.3</p>
<p> -Lagging    104.9   0.3  -0.3  -0.1   0.1  Unch   0.1   0.1</p>
<p>Following are components of the index of leading indicators with net contributions to monthly changes.</p>
<p>    -			March    Feb (Prev)   Jan (Prev)   Dec</p>
<p> Average Workweek	 0.07   0.07  0.07  -0.10 -0.10   0.10</p>
<p> Initial Jobless Claims Unch   0.10  0.10   0.11  0.11  -0.07</p>
<p> Consumer Goods Orders -0.05   0.06  0.05   0.15  0.13  -0.06</p>
<p> Slower Deliveries	0.07   0.10  0.10  -0.11 -0.11   Unch</p>
<p> Capital Goods Orders  -0.04   0.03  0.03   0.04  0.03   Unch</p>
<p> Building Permits	 0.01   0.03  0.03  -0.02 -0.02   Unch</p>
<p> Stock Prices	    -0.02   0.08  0.08   0.06  0.06   0.02</p>
<p> Money Supply	     0.06   0.03  0.03   0.06  0.06   0.09</p>
<p> Treasury Yield Curve   0.01  -0.02 -0.02   0.06  0.06   0.02</p>
<p> Consumer Expectations -0.02   0.04  0.04  -0.01 -0.01  -0.03</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected March leading indicators to rise 0.2 percent.</p>
</text>
